# Purpose
Keep navigation stable and type-safe using Expo Router's file-based routing model.

## Do / Don't

### DO
DO follow file-based routing:
  - Route screens live under app/
  - Navigation structure defined by _layout.*
  - Dynamic params via [param] segments
DO enable and use Typed Routes if the project supports it:
  - Configure typed routes in app config and use Expo CLI generation.
  - Prefer typed <Link /> hrefs and typed navigation APIs where available.
DO validate route params at runtime:
  - Treat params as unknown/string, narrow safely before use.

### DON'T
MUST NOT rename/move route files without:
  - **BREAKING** label
  - migration notes (links, deep links, notifications, bookmarks)
MUST NOT parse params unsafely (no unguarded Number(param); guard NaN/undefined).
MUST NOT place shared components/utilities inside app/ unless the repo already does so intentionally.

## Completion Checklist
[ ] Route changes match Expo Router conventions (app/, _layout.*, dynamic segments).
[ ] Typed routes are used where available; params still runtime-validated.
[ ] Any route rename is labeled BREAKING with migration notes.
[ ] Navigation flows exercised (push/back; relevant screens render without param crashes).

## Common Pitfalls
Silent route renames breaking deep links and saved URLs.
Using params before they exist on first render.
Mixing navigation patterns inconsistently.
